usage: llm_matrix_tool.py [-h] [--model MODELS] [--models-file MODELS_FILE]
                          [--failures-only] [--source-log SOURCE_LOG]
                          [--limit LIMIT] [--min-context MIN_CONTEXT]
                          [--max-context MAX_CONTEXT]
                          [--probe-timeout PROBE_TIMEOUT]
                          [--remote-timeout REMOTE_TIMEOUT] [--optimize]
                          [--optimize-only] [--host HOST]
                          [--provider PROVIDER]
                          [--configure-harness {opencode}]
                          [--target-host TARGET_HOST]
                          [--target-user TARGET_USER]
                          [--source-host SOURCE_HOST]
                          [--source-server {lmstudio}]
                          [--selection {powerful,fastest,specific}]
                          [--specific-model SPECIFIC_MODEL]
                          [--base-url BASE_URL] [--context CONTEXT]
                          [--skip-load] [--install-harness]
                          [--configure-dry-run]

Run the LM Studio model matrix, optimize working models, or configure agent
harness model routes.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --model MODELS        Model ref to test; repeatable.
  --models-file MODELS_FILE
                        JSON sidecar describing selected models and run
                        options.
  --failures-only       Select only failing models from a prior run log.
  --source-log SOURCE_LOG
                        Prior matrix log to mine for failures.
  --limit LIMIT         Limit the selected model list to the first N entries.
  --min-context MIN_CONTEXT
                        Lowest context to try when ratcheting.
  --max-context MAX_CONTEXT
                        Highest context to try when ratcheting or optimizing.
  --probe-timeout PROBE_TIMEOUT
                        Timeout seconds for each opencode probe.
  --remote-timeout REMOTE_TIMEOUT
                        Timeout seconds for each remote lms command.
  --optimize            Run optimize_llm_performance after a model
                        successfully probes.
  --optimize-only       Skip first-pass matrix run and run only
                        optimize_llm_performance on the selected models.
  --host HOST           Only probe models on this host (e.g., framemoowork,
                        moosacrem1promax).
  --provider PROVIDER   Only probe models from this opencode provider name.
  --configure-harness {opencode}
                        Configure a target agent harness with a selected model
                        route.
  --target-host TARGET_HOST
                        Target host to configure. Defaults to local machine.
  --target-user TARGET_USER
                        Target user account for harness config.
  --source-host SOURCE_HOST
                        Model server host, usually an LM Studio host.
  --source-server {lmstudio}
                        Model server type for harness configuration.
  --selection {powerful,fastest,specific}
                        Model selection policy for harness configuration.
  --specific-model SPECIFIC_MODEL
                        Specific backend model id to configure when
                        --selection specific is used.
  --base-url BASE_URL   Known OpenAI-compatible base URL. If omitted, discover
                        from the target host.
  --context CONTEXT     Context length to load on the source model server.
  --skip-load           Do not load the selected model on the source server
                        before writing/verifying config.
  --install-harness     Install or repair the target harness CLI when
                        supported.
  --configure-dry-run   Print planned harness config without writing remote
                        files.
